== Title / identity audit ==

Two queued titles were normalized during capture:

* [[Generalization]] → [[Generalization (machine learning)]]
* [[Data leakage]] → [[Data leakage (machine learning)]]

The first avoids collision with durable meanings of generalization across logic, psychology, linguistics and mathematics.

The second avoids collision with computer-security/privacy data leakage.

[[Spurious correlation]], [[Distribution shift]], and [[Benchmark contamination]] remain unqualified because their useful public scope is broader than one model family and their intended identity is sufficiently specific.

“Fitting bias” was rejected as a canonical concept.

No duplicate [[Learning]], [[Correlation]], [[Selection bias]], [[Validation]], [[Probability]], or [[Cognitive bias]] identity was created.

